Java 7 Pipe Symbol (|) – Multi-Catch Exception Handling
(Category / Case based explanation)
What is Pipe Symbol Concept?

Introduced in Java 7

Used in catch block

Allows handling multiple exceptions in a single catch block

Called Multi-catch

Syntax
try {
    // risky code
}
catch (Exception1 | Exception2 | Exception3 e) {
    // handling code
}

CASE 1️⃣: Pipe Symbol with Unchecked Exceptions
(Runtime / Automatic Exceptions)
Key Points

Unchecked exceptions need NOT be present in try block

Compiler does NOT check them

Program compiles even if try block never throws them

Common Unchecked Exceptions

ArithmeticException

NullPointerException

NumberFormatException

ClassCastException

StringIndexOutOfBoundsException

Example
try {
    int x = 10 / 0;   // ArithmeticException
}
catch (ArithmeticException |
       NullPointerException |
       NumberFormatException e) {

    System.out.println("Exception handled");
}


✅ Valid
Even though only ArithmeticException can occur, others are allowed.

CASE 2️⃣: Pipe Symbol with Checked Exceptions
(Compile-time Exceptions)
Key Rule ⭐

👉 Checked exceptions MUST have a chance to occur in try block

Common Checked Exceptions

InterruptedException

FileNotFoundException

IOException

❌ Invalid Example
try {
    Thread.sleep(1000);   // only InterruptedException
}
catch (InterruptedException | FileNotFoundException e) {
    System.out.println("Handled");
}


❌ Compile-time Error

FileNotFoundException is never thrown in try block

✅ Valid Example
try {
    Thread.sleep(1000);
    FileInputStream fis = new FileInputStream("abc.txt");
}
catch (InterruptedException | FileNotFoundException e) {
    System.out.println("Handled");
}


✔ Both checked exceptions have a chance to occur

CASE 3️⃣: Mixing Checked + Unchecked Exceptions
(Allowed ✅)
Rules

You CAN mix checked & unchecked exceptions

Checked exception MUST be possible in try block

Unchecked exception presence is optional

Example
try {
    Thread.sleep(1000);   // Checked
    int x = 10 / 0;       // Unchecked
}
catch (InterruptedException | ArithmeticException e) {
    System.out.println("Handled");
}


✅ Valid

InterruptedException → present in try

ArithmeticException → allowed automatically

CASE 4️⃣: Parent & Child Exception in Pipe Symbol
(NOT Allowed ❌)
Rule ⭐⭐

👉 Cannot combine Parent and Child exception together

Example
try {
    FileInputStream fis = new FileInputStream("abc.txt");
}
catch (IOException | FileNotFoundException e) {
    System.out.println("Handled");
}


❌ Compile-time Error

FileNotFoundException is subclass of IOException

Reason

Parent already handles child

Child becomes useless

✅ Correct Way
catch (FileNotFoundException e) { }


OR

catch (IOException e) { }
