diffference between noclassdeffoundError and classnotfoundException
| ClassNotFoundException                                                  | NoClassDefFoundError                                                                   |
| ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| It is an **Exception**                                                  | It is an **Error**                                                                     |
| It is a **Checked Exception**                                           | It is an **Unchecked Error**                                                           |
| Happens when JVM **cannot find the class while loading it dynamically** | Happens when JVM **found the class during compile time but cannot find it at runtime** |
| Mostly occurs with `Class.forName()`                                    | Mostly occurs because `.class` file or dependency is missing                           |
| We can handle it using `try-catch` or `throws`                          | Usually fixed by correcting classpath/dependencies                                     |
| Example: Class name typed wrong                                         | Example: JAR removed after build                                                       |
